out/

# mach dep checkouts materialized by `mach dep pull`; mach.lock is the source of truth
dep/

# res/spv/ is NOT ignored. The compiled SPIR-V is committed, because a consumer
# that pulls boom over git has to have it: the modules are #[embed]ed, and an
# embed is not a build-graph edge, so nothing runs the build-shaders step on a
# consumer's behalf (mach#2887). Ignoring them made boom unbuildable as a
# dependency while every example, which resolves boom by path into a tree that
# had been built locally, kept working.
#
# They are also asset-shaped rather than output-shaped: SPIR-V is
# target-independent, so one copy serves every target and profile, which is why
# they live under res/ and not under out/. CI asserts they match a fresh build.

# generated at runtime by examples/audio, not assets
*.wav

# An example's compiled shaders are generated by its own build-shaders step and
# regenerate on a clean checkout, which examples/shader is built from in CI. Not
# the same case as boom's own res/spv above, which is committed because a
# consumer pulling boom over git has no step that would produce it.
/examples/*/res/spv/
